---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const base = '/prisma-to-sql';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Query examples - prisma-sql"
  description="Filters, relation filters, include trees, pagination, cursor pagination, aggregates and groupBy with prisma-sql."
  active={`${base}/docs/queries`}
>
  <h1>Query examples</h1>
  <p>All examples use the standard Prisma API. prisma-sql converts supported shapes to SQL; everything else falls back to Prisma.</p>

  <h2>Filters</h2>
  <pre><code>{`{ age: { gt: 18, lte: 65 } }
{ status: { in: ['ACTIVE', 'PENDING'] } }
{ status: { notIn: ['DELETED'] } }

{ email: { contains: '@example.com' } }
{ email: { startsWith: 'user' } }
{ email: { endsWith: '.com' } }
{ email: { contains: 'EXAMPLE', mode: 'insensitive' } }

{ AND: [{ status: 'ACTIVE' }, { verified: true }] }
{ OR: [{ role: 'ADMIN' }, { role: 'MODERATOR' }] }
{ NOT: { status: 'DELETED' } }

{ deletedAt: null }
{ deletedAt: { not: null } }`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Relations</h2>
  <pre><code>{`{
  include: {
    posts: true,
    profile: true,
  },
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>Nested includes support <code>where</code>, <code>orderBy</code> and <code>take</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  include: {
    posts: {
      where: { published: true },
      orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
      take: 5,
      include: {
        comments: true,
      },
    },
  },
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Relation list filters</h3>
  <pre><code>{`{ where: { posts: { some: { published: true } } } }
{ where: { posts: { every: { published: true } } } }
{ where: { posts: { none: { published: false } } } }`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Pagination and ordering</h2>
  <pre><code>{`{
  take: 10,
  skip: 20,
  orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
}

{
  cursor: { id: 100 },
  skip: 1,
  take: 10,
  orderBy: { id: 'asc' },
}

{
  orderBy: [
    { status: 'asc' },
    { priority: 'desc' },
    { createdAt: 'desc' },
  ],
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Composite cursor pagination</h3>
  <p>Use an <code>orderBy</code> that starts with the cursor fields in the same order. This matches keyset pagination expectations and avoids unstable page boundaries.</p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  cursor: { tenantId: 10, id: 500 },
  skip: 1,
  take: 20,
  orderBy: [
    { tenantId: 'asc' },
    { id: 'asc' },
  ],
}`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Optional relation null ordering</h3>
  <p>
    A required scalar reached through an optional to-one relation can use <code>{'{ sort, nulls }'}</code>, because the
    relation's <code>LEFT JOIN</code> makes the SQL expression nullable. Queries using this form execute through
    prisma-sql; if acceleration fails they return an explicit "prisma-sql cannot fall back" error instead of forwarding
    input Prisma would reject.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`await prisma.jobAd.findMany({
  orderBy: {
    boost: {
      boostedUntil: { sort: 'desc', nulls: 'last' },
    },
  },
})`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Aggregates</h2>
  <pre><code>{`await prisma.user.count({
  where: { status: 'ACTIVE' },
})

await prisma.task.aggregate({
  where: { status: 'DONE' },
  _count: { _all: true },
  _sum: { estimatedHours: true },
  _avg: { estimatedHours: true },
  _min: { startedAt: true },
  _max: { completedAt: true },
})`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Aggregate values are mapped back to Prisma-style types — <code>Decimal</code>, <code>BigInt</code>,
    <code>DateTime</code> and <code>_count</code> keep their expected value types.
  </p>

  <h2>groupBy</h2>
  <pre><code>{`await prisma.task.groupBy({
  by: ['status', 'priority'],
  _count: { _all: true },
  _avg: { estimatedHours: true },
  having: {
    status: {
      _count: { gte: 5 },
    },
  },
})`}</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
